FINDINGS:
1. [BLOCKER] tests/keyword_reservation_test.rs:133 — REACHABLE `return` row snippet `to answer() / give back 1 / end` contains no `return` word, so the behavioural half never exercises `return` and breaking `return` keeps the suite green — fix by using a snippet that contains `return`, e.g. `to f() / return 1 / end`.
2. [MAJOR] tests/keyword_reservation_test.rs:55 — `parse_error` uses `Lexer::tokenize(source).ok()` so a lexer failure becomes `None` (treated as parsed), and the REACHABLE loop at 219-226 passes on lex failure — fix by propagating the lex error and failing the test on `Err`.
3. [MAJOR] src/parser.rs:435 — `Parser::expect` still formats `Expected {:?} but got {:?}` with Debug `TokenKind`, bypassing the new `word_for` humanization, so missing `to`/`then`/`end` still leak internal names like `To`/`Then`/`End` — fix by routing `expect` through `word_for`/`unexpected_token`.
4. [MAJOR] src/lexer.rs:350 — `word_for` maps shared kinds by kind alone, so operator tokens misreport as keywords (`%` at src/lexer.rs:433 produces `Mod` but prints `'mod'`; `!` at src/lexer.rs:507 produces `Not` but prints `'not'`; `GiveBack` at src/lexer.rs:44 always prints `'give'` even for `'back'`) — fix by mapping by token origin or splitting the kinds.
5. [MAJOR] tests/keyword_reservation_test.rs:86 — enumeration is a raw text scan `PARSER_SOURCE.contains("TokenKind::X")` (repeated at 493 for the other-phases guard), so a comment mentioning the kind satisfies it with no reachable parser arm — fix by stripping comments/strings before scanning or asserting behavioural reachability for every word.
6. [MAJOR] docs/GRAMMAR.md:509 — grammar still promises freed words as syntax (`object_literal = 'new' ...`, example `set person to new Person` at :580, `when_statement` at :228, `async_function`/`parallel_block` with `wait`/`done` at :346-351) while the lexer emits identifiers, and the §1.3 note at :60-62 falsely claims they are no longer described; SPEC.md:989 still documents `ask "Your name?"` — fix by updating/removing those productions and examples and extending the doc-agreement test beyond §1.3.
7. [MINOR] src/lexer.rs:88 — `TokenKind::By` is dead: no `KEYWORDS` entry or lexer arm ever produces it, yet src/parser.rs:944 matches it, so one arm of the step-marker check is unreachable — fix by removing the variant or reserving `by`.
8. [MINOR] src/parser.rs:769 — `parse_constant` (`Expected constant name after 'constant'`) and `parse_export` at :1500 stay generic instead of routing through `expected_name`, so `constant if ...`/`export if` do not name the word unlike `set`/`import` — fix by routing both through `expected_name`.
9. [MINOR] phases/phase-049/REPORT.md:120 — gate arithmetic does not add up (`1410 passed, was 1408 before this run's two added tests` for a 13-test new file) and :11 claims the async productions were `removed` while docs/GRAMMAR.md:346-351 keeps them with a note — fix by correcting the counts and the wording.
